okay today I'm going to talk to you  about ecosystems an ecosystem is a  community of living things along with  all the nonliving things in an area  where they live an example of an  ecosystem could be a jungle  a woodland or even something as small as  a pond in fact the example that we're  going to look at today is of a pond so  here's just the lay of the water at the  top of the pond now the first term that  we're going to learn is the term  individual because what we're doing is  we're learning the different layers of  an ecosystem now an individual in an  ecosystem is a single organism such as  this little fish here so an organism is  the scientific term for a living thing  so as you can see there's just one  particular organism here one fish so  that is the very most basic level of the  ecosystem the individual what we're  going to do now is we're going to look  at the next level of the ecosystem which  is called a population now a population  is the total number of one particular  species within an ecosystem so as you  can see these fish are all the same  species right here a species all that it  means is a group of similar organisms  that are similar enough in order to be  able to reproduce to have fertile  offspring so as you can see this  population is just made of one  particular species so that's the next  layer of this ecosystem so if we have a  look at the next level the next level is  a community now what a community is is a  community is made of a few different  species of organisms so organisms of a  different species we're living within  this habitat a habitat is just a place  to live so let's say we've got a  different species of fish  and remember as well an organism is a  living thing o organism is a living  thing  but it's not just animals it could also  be plants so let's have a look at this  if I just do these Reed's here so as you  can see a community is all of the  organisms all of the living things  within a particular habitat this is  consisting of both animals and plants so  now we're just going to have a look at  the final level of an ecosystem which is  the whole ecosystem itself the complete  ecosystem is all the living things and  the nonliving things so if I was to just  draw a few rocks here because this is  the the nonliving parts of the ecosystem  as well maybe we've just got some some  of the ground here the water itself the  light the whole thing altogether  everything combined is the entire  ecosystem in this particular context the  ecosystem is the pond  so just to recap an individual organism  is just a single living thing a  population is made up of one particular  species it's the total number of one  particular species a community is all of  the different living things so all of  the different organisms within this  habitat and finally the ecosystem is all  the living things and the nonliving  things combined that is the introduction  to the ecosystems thank you
 

